# Content markdown

All site copy lives under `content/`. Frontmatter is `key: value` (one line per key). Body is markdown where applicable.

## `content/home.md`

Controls homepage sections and preview counts:

```yaml
---
name: Shubh Gupta
headline: Hi. I make things.
bio: ...
projectsLabel: What I'm working on
writingPreviewCount: 4
historyPreviewCount: 10
galleryUrl: /gallery
historyUrl: /history
---
```

## `content/projects/*.md`

Required: `title`, `description`, `href`. Optional: `role`, `year`, `tip`, `order` (lower = first).

## `content/blog/*.md`

Required: `title`, `description`, `date` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`). Body supports `##`, lists, links, blockquotes via `MarkdownArticle`.

## `content/gallery.md`

Frontmatter: `url`, `cloudinaryBase`, `intro`. Body lines:

```
id | cloudinary-filename.jpg | tile title | /p/0 | feature
```

Layout suffix: `feature` | `tall` | `wide` | omit for square.

## `content/timeline.md`

Frontmatter: `title`, `description`. Body:

```
- **2026-08-18** — Ships [wolfpdf](https://github.com/...), description
```

## `content/pages/*.md`

Frontmatter: `title`, `description`, `heading`. Body = trust page prose.

## After adding content

New blog slugs auto-SSG via `generateStaticParams`. New routes need `src/app/` page + `src/app/sitemap.ts` entry.
